**What was implemented:** `encode(numbers)` converts each int into 7-bit groups, emitting MSB-first with bit #7 (`0x80`) set on every byte except the last; `decode(bytes_)` accumulates 7 bits per byte, emitting a number when the continuation bit is clear, and raises `ValueError("incomplete byte sequence")` if the last byte still has the continuation bit set. All 12 spec examples, decode cases, edge cases, and 11 round-trips verified by executed assertions (exit 0).
